 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+Specifies the maximum number of ranges to return, unset (no limit) by default.
+When the header contains more valid ranges than `limit` (counted after
+`combine` is applied, if enabled), they are not rejected or truncated; instead
+they are merged into a single range from the lowest start to the highest end.
+Any gaps between the original ranges are included in the merged range.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(200, 'bytes=0-10,50-60,100-120', { limit: 2 })
+// => [
+//      { start: 0, end: 120 }
+//    ]
+```
+
